{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773177817,"nonce":"+qWDBwnvxWYqikMYFpzX8pwRctA=","title":"CLAUDE.md: clarify auth request cwd for repos where protected branch lives in a worktree","message":"The global CLAUDE.md says \"cwd must always be the main worktree\", using .dotfiles as the example. For repos like feedbax where the protected branch (develop) lives in worktrees/develop/ rather than the main worktree (which is on main), this instruction is ambiguous and leads to the wrong cwd being set. The correct rule is: cwd must be the worktree where the protected branch is checked out. For .dotfiles that is the main worktree; for feedbax it is worktrees/develop/. Update CLAUDE.md (global) to make this explicit, either in the auth request section or as a feedbax-specific note in feedbax/CLAUDE.md.","files":null}]}